{"id":4358,"date":"2025-03-20T05:29:00","date_gmt":"2025-03-19T23:59:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/?p=4358"},"modified":"2025-03-20T05:29:00","modified_gmt":"2025-03-19T23:59:00","slug":"tmj-symptoms-and-treatment","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-symptoms-and-treatment\/","title":{"rendered":"What Causes TMJ Disorders? TMJ Symptoms and Treatment"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>In this article, we will understand what causes TMJ disorders, its symptoms, and its treatment. If you are looking for the right guidance and expert treatment for your TMJ-related issues, then Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the best TMJ specialists in the country. You can reach out to her for consultation by calling her at&nbsp;<em><a href=\"tel:+919884520520\">9884 520 520<\/a><\/em>.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ or Temporomandibular Joint is the joint that connects the jaw to the temporal bones of the skull that are located just in front of each ear. And any condition that affects these joints, the muscles controlling these jaw movements, and the surrounding nerves, are referred to as TMJ disorders. These are some of the most important and complex joints in the human body as these are the joints responsible for chewing, speaking, and facial expressions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To ensure that TMJ disorders are effectively treated it is important to recognize the TMJ symptoms at an early stage. So let\u2019s understand the causes, and symptoms of TMJ and the different treatment methods available for people.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A good starting point is to get your consultation done by a TMJ expert. And Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the best <a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialists-in-india\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialists-in-india\/\">TMJ specialists in the world<\/a>. She brings more than 15 years of experience to the table along with a very patient-centric approach to her treatment.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What causes TMJ?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The causes of TMJ can be one among many. From muscle tension to joint dysfunction to habits that put a lot of pressure on your jaw. Let\u2019s understand some of these causes:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Stress:<\/strong>&nbsp;Stress is not just a psychological state of mind, but it also has some very tangible physical effects, specifically on the TMJ. When people experience stress, the brain sends descending signals through the nervous system, which is its way of a fight or flight response. One of the physical reactions to this is the tightening of the muscles around TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>This, in turn, leads to those muscles becoming taut, which means the muscles become tight and stay in the same state. This leads to discomfort, pain, and changes in the normal function of the joint.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Accidents:<\/strong>&nbsp;Direct trauma to your jaw, like a heavy blow or an injury, can damage the joint structure. Accidents like whiplash from sudden neck movements, such as car accidents, can potentially damage the TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sports injuries:<\/strong>&nbsp;Contact sports or activities with the risk of facial injury can lead to TMJ disorders.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Osteoarthritis:<\/strong>&nbsp;The wear and tear of ageing can lead to the degeneration of the joint cartilage, affecting its functionality.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rheumatoid arthritis:<\/strong>&nbsp;This autoimmune disease can attack the synovial membrane that lines the TMJ, leading to inflammation and joint damage.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A common misconception is that bruxism (teeth grinding), jaw clenching, bite problems, teeth misalignment, or wisdom teeth can be a cause of TMJ, but recent discoveries have proved that teeth are not related to TMJ disorders. Even though they were widely believed issues, researchers and the latest studies have disproved them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">TMJ Symptoms: Recognizing the Signs<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders can cause a variety of symptoms, ranging from mild discomfort to severe pain and dysfunction. Recognizing these signs is the first step toward getting the right care.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common Symptoms<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Jaw pain and tenderness:<\/strong>&nbsp;This is one of the most noticeable symptoms and the pain can be constant or it might come and go. It can also worsen by jaw movements such as chewing or speaking.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Difficulty opening or closing the mouth:<\/strong>&nbsp;TMJ disorders can lead to a limited range of motion in the jaw, making it hard to open or close the mouth fully.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Clicking, popping, or grating sounds in the jaw joint:&nbsp;<\/strong>These sounds might occur with jaw movement and, although they can be painless, they indicate dysfunction in the TMJ.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Symptoms That May Be Overlooked<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ear aches or ringing in the ears (tinnitus):<\/strong>&nbsp;Because of the TMJ&#8217;s proximity to the ear canal, disorders can cause ear-related symptoms<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Headaches and migraines:&nbsp;<\/strong>TMJ disorders can trigger pain that radiates into the temples, forehead, or back of the head, often mimicking tension headaches or migraines.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Neck and shoulder pain:<\/strong>&nbsp;The muscles around the TMJ connect to those in the neck and shoulders, so TMJ dysfunction can lead to tension and pain in these areas.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Teeth Pain:<\/strong>&nbsp;Sometimes &#8216;pain from the muscles gets to the teeth and it feels like the patient has teeth pain. But more often than not it\u2019s the muscles surrounding TMJ that is the real cause.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Impact of TMJ Symptoms on Quality of Life<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders can significantly impact daily life, affecting one&#8217;s ability to eat, speak, and sleep comfortably. Chronic pain can lead to difficulties in concentration, mood changes, and overall reduced quality of life.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Diagnosing TMJ Disorders<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Proper diagnosis is crucial for effective treatment. Diagnosing TMJ disorders involves a combination of medical history, physical examination, and possibly imaging tests.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">When to See a Healthcare Professional<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Individuals experiencing persistent jaw pain, difficulty in moving the jaw, or other related symptoms should consult a <a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/what-kind-of-doctor-treats-tmj-pain\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/what-kind-of-doctor-treats-tmj-pain\/\">doctor who can treats TMJ<\/a>. Early intervention can prevent further complications.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Types of Professionals Who Diagnose and Treat TMJ<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Orofacial Pain Specialist:&nbsp;<\/strong>Orofacial pain specialists are dentists who have gained additional expertise in managing mouth, jaw and face pain. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the best Orofacial pain specialists in the country, with 15+ years of experience in this industry and a very holistic approach to the whole pain relief process. These orofacial specialists usually include medication, physical therapy and behavioural strategies in their treatment.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar\u2019s approach is backed by her experience and innovation in the field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"1\">\n<li>The first stage of the treatment involves the identification of muscle tightness.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Then, she relieves the trigger points using trigger point injections.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>This is then followed by physical therapy and ultrasound injection in the Lateral Pterygoid muscle.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">She is the only specialist in India to follow this approach to pain relief, and many satisfied patients are a testament to its effective nature.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Dentists:<\/strong>&nbsp;Often the first point of contact, dentists can assess for bite issues and signs of bruxism.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Oral surgeons (maxillofacial surgeons):<\/strong>&nbsp;Specialists in facial bone, teeth, and jaw surgery, they can provide advanced treatments for TMJ disorders.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Physical therapists:<\/strong>&nbsp;They can offer exercises and treatments to reduce pain and improve the function of the jaw.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Diagnostic Tests and Procedures<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Physical examination:&nbsp;<\/strong>Checking for pain or tenderness in the jaw, clicking, popping, or difficulty moving the joint.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Imaging tests:&nbsp;<\/strong>X-rays, MRIs, and CT scans can provide detailed images of the jaw and TMJ to assess the extent of the disorder.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Diagnostic criteria:<\/strong>&nbsp;Healthcare professionals use specific criteria to diagnose TMJ disorders, including patient history, clinical examination, and imaging results.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Treatment Options for TMJ Disorders<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Treatment for TMJ disorders can vary from conservative home care to more invasive surgical interventions, depending on the severity of the condition.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Non-surgical Treatments<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Lifestyle modifications and home remedies:&nbsp;<\/strong>Stress reduction, jaw exercises, and avoiding hard or chewy foods can help alleviate symptoms.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Medications:<\/strong>&nbsp;Over-the-counter pain relievers, anti-inflammatories, and muscle relaxants can be used to manage pain and inflammation.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Oral appliances:&nbsp;<\/strong>Mouth guards or splints can help reduce clenching and grinding, alleviating stress on the TMJ.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Surgical Treatments (When Necessary)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Arthrocentesis:<\/strong>&nbsp;A minimally invasive procedure where fluid is injected into the joint to remove debris and inflammatory byproducts.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Arthroscopy:<\/strong>&nbsp;A procedure involving a small camera inserted into the joint space to remove inflamed tissue or realign the disc.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Open-joint surgery:&nbsp;<\/strong>In severe cases, surgery might be needed to repair or replace the joint.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Alternative and Complementary Therapies<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Acupuncture:<\/strong>&nbsp;This traditional Chinese medicine technique can help relieve pain and improve jaw function.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Biofeedback:<\/strong>&nbsp;Using monitoring devices to become more aware of the body&#8217;s physiological responses to stress, with the aim of learning to control them.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Massage therapy:<\/strong>&nbsp;Focusing on the jaw, head, and neck muscles can help alleviate tension and pain.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preventing TMJ Disorders<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While not all cases of TMJ disorders can be prevented, especially those related to genetic predisposition or unavoidable trauma, there are steps individuals can take to minimize their risk and maintain healthy TMJ function.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tips for Maintaining TMJ Health<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Practice good posture:<\/strong>&nbsp;Poor posture, especially a forward head position, can strain the muscles of the neck and jaw. Maintaining a neutral spine can help alleviate this strain.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Avoid excessive jaw movements:&nbsp;<\/strong>Habits like gum chewing, nail-biting, or biting on hard objects can overwork the TMJ and lead to discomfort.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Use proper techniques to yawn:<\/strong>&nbsp;Supporting the jaw during wide yawns can prevent overextension of the TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Stress management:&nbsp;<\/strong>Since stress can lead to jaw clenching and teeth grinding, techniques such as deep breathing, yoga, or meditation can be beneficial.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Importance of Regular Dental Check-ups<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Regular visits to the dentist can help catch early signs of TMJ disorders, such as teeth wear from grinding or bite misalignments. Dentists can also provide guidance on oral appliances that can prevent or reduce symptoms.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Avoiding Behaviors That Strain the TMJ<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Being conscious of habits that put undue stress on the TMJ and actively working to modify these behaviors can go a long way in preventing TMJ disorders. Education on proper jaw alignment and muscle relaxation can also be instrumental.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">&nbsp;Living with TMJ: Management and Support<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For those already dealing with TMJ disorders, management focuses on reducing pain, improving function, and enhancing quality of life.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Coping Strategies for Managing Chronic TMJ Pain<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living with chronic pain requires a multifaceted approach. This can include physical therapy exercises to strengthen and relax the jaw muscles, applying heat or cold to reduce pain and swelling, and adopting a soft food diet to minimize jaw strain.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Support Groups and Resources<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finding support among others who are dealing with TMJ disorders can provide emotional relief and valuable tips. Many online and community-based support groups exist, offering a platform to share experiences and coping strategies.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Role of Mental Health in Managing TMJ Disorders<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Chronic pain can have significant mental health impacts, including anxiety and depression. Addressing these psychological aspects is crucial for holistic TMJ management. Counseling, cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT), and other mental health services can be vital components of a comprehensive treatment plan.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Dietary Adjustments for TMJ Relief<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You are what you eat, so making changes to one&#8217;s diet can significantly impact TMJ discomfort. Opting for soft foods that require minimal chewing can give the jaw a rest and reduce strain. Avoiding sticky, chewy, or hard foods that can exacerbate TMJ symptoms is also advisable. When necessary, cutting food into smaller pieces can help minimize the effort needed to chew.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Ergonomics and Workspace Modifications<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is such a common practice to slouch over our chairs at the workplace. Even now, most of you would be reading this while being in a very non ergonomic posture.&nbsp;Poor posture, especially while sitting for long periods, can contribute to TMJ pain. Adjusting the workspace to promote good posture can help alleviate some of this strain. This might include using an ergonomic chair, ensuring the computer screen is at eye level, and taking regular breaks to stretch and move.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Relaxation Techniques Beyond Stress Management<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Incorporating relaxation techniques into your daily routine can help manage the stress that often exacerbates TMJ symptoms. Techniques such as guided imagery, deep breathing exercises, and progressive muscle relaxation can reduce overall tension and provide relief.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Importance of Regular Follow-ups with Healthcare Providers<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Managing TMJ disorders is often an ongoing process that requires adjustments to treatment plans over time. Regular follow-ups with healthcare providers ensure that treatments remain effective and are adjusted as needed. These appointments are also opportunities to discuss any new symptoms or concerns.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Educating Friends and Family<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Educating friends and family about TMJ disorders can garner support and understanding from one&#8217;s social circle. Sharing information about the condition can help others recognize the challenges associated with TMJ and provide appropriate support.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Exploring Professional Counseling<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living with chronic pain, like that from TMJ disorders, can be mentally and emotionally taxing. Professional counseling or therapy can offer strategies to cope with the emotional aspects of chronic pain, improving overall well-being.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders consist of a wide range of conditions that can overall affect a person\u2019s quality of life. But with the right knowledge about the condition, its symptoms, its effects, its prevention, and its treatment, we can ensure the right pain management and overall better quality of life.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That is why the right consultation at the beginning is so important. Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the pioneers in this field in this country. She has more than 15 years of experience in the field and has a patient-centric approach to ensure the patients are comfortable, well-briefed, and have a customized approach.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">She encourages everyone to not ignore the signs of TMJ disorders, and see their healthcare professional at the first sign of any disorder. This first step towards professional help can make a huge difference as they are well-versed in ongoing research and the new treatment options available in the market.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So with this knowledge, we hope you\u2019ll be well aware, and take the right steps at the right time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Take care and Godspeed!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">TMJ Symptoms and Treatment FAQs<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Who is the best TMJ specialist in India?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one the best TMJ specialists in India with more than 15 years of experience in the field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>What are the early signs of TMJ disorders I should watch out for?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Early signs can include jaw pain or tenderness, a clicking or popping sound when opening or closing the mouth, difficulty chewing, and discomfort around the ear area. If you notice these symptoms persistently, it might be time to consult a healthcare professional.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Can TMJ disorders go away on their own, or will I always need treatment?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some milder cases of TMJ disorders, particularly those caused by temporary stress or strain, can improve on their own with self-care practices like jaw exercises, stress reduction, and avoiding excessive jaw movements. However, persistent or severe cases may require professional treatment to prevent worsening of symptoms.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Are there any specific exercises I can do at home to relieve TMJ pain?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, there are several jaw exercises and <a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-exercises-for-pain-relief\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-exercises-for-pain-relief\/\">relaxation techniques that can help alleviate TMJ pain<\/a>. These might include gentle stretching exercises to improve range of motion, strengthening exercises to improve jaw stability, and relaxation techniques to reduce muscle tension. It&#8217;s important to consult with a healthcare professional before starting any new exercise regimen.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>How can I differentiate TMJ pain from other types of facial pain or headaches?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ pain is often localized around the jaw joint and might be accompanied by clicking or popping sounds, limited jaw movement, and muscle tenderness. It can also radiate towards the ear, cheek, and temple. Unlike other facial pains or headaches, TMJ pain is closely related to jaw movement and function. A healthcare professional can help accurately diagnose the source of your pain.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Is surgery a common treatment for TMJ disorders, and what are the risks?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Surgery is generally considered a last resort for TMJ disorders and is only recommended when other non-invasive treatments have failed to relieve symptoms. The risks of TMJ surgery can include infection, nerve injury, and potential worsening of symptoms. It&#8217;s crucial to discuss all possible treatment options and their risks with a healthcare professional before deciding on surgery.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>In this article, we will understand what causes TMJ disorders, its symptoms, and its treatment. If you are looking for the right guidance and expert treatment for your TMJ-related issues, then Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the best TMJ specialists in the country. You can reach out to her for consultation by calling [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[48],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4358","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-tmj"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4358","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/2"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4358"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4358\/revisions"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre